&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Or over HTTPS, since v0.9.0, with &lt;code&gt;tls = true&lt;/code&gt; and a&lt;a href="https://go-fileshare.github.io/docs/0.51/security/tls/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tls&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-hcl" data-lang="hcl"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;serve&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;s3&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; addr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;0.0.0.0:9000&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; tls&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The fifth protocol, and the one that makes an image reachable from anything
that speaks object storage — a backup tool, a data pipeline, &lt;code&gt;rclone&lt;/code&gt;, a
browser&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;fetch()&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Nothing mounts.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET / the shares this person may use, as buckets
GET /photos?list-type=2 the files in that share, as keys
GET /photos/holiday.jpg the file itself, Range and all&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="a-share-is-a-bucket"&gt;A share is a bucket&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="a-share-is-a-bucket"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#a-share-is-a-bucket" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Served over the &lt;strong&gt;same per-user tree SFTP uses&lt;/strong&gt;: a filesystem whose top level
is the shares this person may use. So a share alice may not use is not a bucket
alice can see, and the access rules are applied in one place rather than copied
into a second protocol.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-blue-200 hx:bg-blue-100 hx:text-blue-900 hx:dark:border-blue-200/30 hx:dark:bg-blue-900/30 hx:dark:text-blue-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A directory inside a share is a prefix, not an object&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which is what S3 clients already believe — they display prefixes ending in
the delimiter as folders. &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; of a directory answers &lt;code&gt;NoSuchKey&lt;/code&gt;, because
answering 200 would make a client think it can fetch the bytes of a folder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="an-access-key-is-a-user-the-secret-key-is-their-password"&gt;An access key is a user; the secret key is their password&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="an-access-key-is-a-user-the-secret-key-is-their-password"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#an-access-key-is-a-user-the-secret-key-is-their-password" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;alice
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;cat alice.pw&lt;span class="k"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;aws --endpoint-url http://attic.example.org:9000 s3 ls&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SigV4 proves possession of the secret by computing an HMAC from it — the
password never crosses the wire, exactly as with NTLMv2.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-red-200 hx:bg-red-100 hx:text-red-900 hx:dark:border-red-200/30 hx:dark:bg-red-900/30 hx:dark:text-red-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M18.364 18.364A9 9 0 005.636 5.636m12.728 12.728A9 9 0 015.636 5.636m12.728 12.728L5.636 5.636"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;So the directory must HOLD the password, not merely check it&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A source that can only &lt;em&gt;verify&lt;/em&gt; a password — an LDAP bind, a bcrypt column— can answer WebDAV and &lt;strong&gt;cannot&lt;/strong&gt; answer S3.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And not an NT hash either: that is the MD4 SMB can work from, and an HMAC
cannot be computed from it. &lt;strong&gt;An identity holding only an NT hash serves
SMB and not S3&lt;/strong&gt; — near neighbours rather than the same answer.&lt;a href="https://go-fileshare.github.io/docs/0.51/configuration/check/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;check&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; prints the column.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⛔ There is no &lt;code&gt;Password()&lt;/code&gt; accessor anywhere in the program: the password is
reached only through &lt;code&gt;Identity.Derive&lt;/code&gt;, which takes a derivation and returns
its result. For S3 the derivation is the identity, because SigV4&amp;rsquo;s key
schedule lives in go-filesystems/s3; the secret goes to that signature check
for that one user and nowhere else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-is-served"&gt;What is served&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-is-served"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-is-served" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;ListBuckets&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;HeadBucket&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ListObjectsV2&lt;/code&gt; with prefix, delimiter, max-keys
and continuation, &lt;code&gt;HeadObject&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;GetObject&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;Range&lt;/code&gt;. SigV4 in both
forms, header and presigned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The object API itself is&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-filesystems/s3" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;go-filesystems/s3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-is-refused-and-why"&gt;What is refused, and why&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-is-refused-and-why"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-is-refused-and-why" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-amber-200 hx:bg-amber-100 hx:text-amber-900 hx:dark:border-amber-200/30 hx:dark:bg-amber-900/30 hx:dark:text-amber-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writes answer 403&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;PUT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt; are refused with &lt;code&gt;AccessDenied&lt;/code&gt; (&amp;ldquo;this export is
read-only&amp;rdquo;). fileshare keeps the S3 server read-only because a share a person
may only read has to refuse at the same place SFTP does, and that is not
wired yet; go-filesystems/s3 v0.3.0, which this release is built on, refuses
every write anyway. Refusing beats a half-written object.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-amber-200 hx:bg-amber-100 hx:text-amber-900 hx:dark:border-amber-200/30 hx:dark:bg-amber-900/30 hx:dark:text-amber-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A bearer token is not accepted here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://go-fileshare.github.io/docs/0.51/protocols/webdav/"&gt;OIDC&lt;/a&gt; works over WebDAV and nowhere else. S3 authenticates with
a SigV4 signature — an HMAC over the request, with no field a bearer token
fits in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The route is STS &lt;code&gt;AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity&lt;/code&gt;, which exchanges an OIDC
token for temporary credentials the client then signs with. It is served on
this listener since v0.50.0: see &lt;a href="#sts"&gt;below&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multipart upload, versioning, ACLs, policies, lifecycle rules, replication and
tagging are not implemented. Setting any of them, and starting a multipart
upload, is a write, and answers &lt;code&gt;AccessDenied&lt;/code&gt; like any other. A &lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; that
asks for one of them (&lt;code&gt;?versioning&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;?acl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;?tagging&lt;/code&gt;&amp;hellip;) is not told apart:the query is ignored and the bucket&amp;rsquo;s listing or the object is returned.&lt;code&gt;NotImplemented&lt;/code&gt; answers a listing other than &lt;code&gt;list-type=2&lt;/code&gt;, any method but&lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt;, and a method no operation here uses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="sts"&gt;Temporary credentials: STS &lt;code&gt;AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="sts"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#sts" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since v0.50.0 the S3 listener also answers the AWS STS API(&lt;code&gt;AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity&lt;/code&gt;, version 2011-06-15): a token from the&lt;a href="https://go-fileshare.github.io/docs/0.51/protocols/webdav/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;oidc&lt;/code&gt; block&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s provider is exchanged for an access key, a secret
key and a session token that &lt;strong&gt;expire&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;code&gt;aws&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;rclone&lt;/code&gt; and the AWS SDKs speak
it as they do to AWS, and nobody holds a password.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-hcl" data-lang="hcl"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;oidc&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; issuer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;https://login.example.org&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; audience&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;fileshare&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;serve&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;s3&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; addr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;0.0.0.0:9000&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; tls&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; sts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; true # POST / with Action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; sts_duration&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;1h&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt; # the default, 15m to 12h
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; sts_max_duration&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;4h&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt; # the most DurationSeconds may ask; defaults to sts_duration
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; static_keys&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt; # no more access-key-is-a-user: only temporary credentials sign
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The token&lt;/strong&gt; is an access token (&lt;code&gt;typ&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;at+jwt&lt;/code&gt;) from the &lt;code&gt;oidc&lt;/code&gt; block&amp;rsquo;s
provider, for that block&amp;rsquo;s issuer and audience — there is no second provider
configuration. A person&amp;rsquo;s token, or a machine&amp;rsquo;s: go-authn/bridge&amp;rsquo;s&lt;code&gt;client_credentials&lt;/code&gt; token for a client that authenticates with a private key(&lt;code&gt;private_key_jwt&lt;/code&gt;) has &lt;code&gt;sub&lt;/code&gt; = the client ID, which is the name here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⛔ &lt;strong&gt;It passes the same rule as a token over WebDAV.&lt;/strong&gt; A valid token for a name
no source here knows is refused unless &lt;code&gt;trust_all = true&lt;/code&gt; or a share&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;oidc:&lt;/code&gt;
rule names it (&lt;code&gt;allow = [&amp;quot;oidc:user:winpc-17&amp;quot;]&lt;/code&gt;). The share&amp;rsquo;s rules then
decide what is visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The answer&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;code&gt;AccessKeyId&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;ASIA…&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;SecretAccessKey&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SessionToken&lt;/code&gt;
and &lt;code&gt;Expiration&lt;/code&gt;. Requests are signed with them and carry the session token in&lt;code&gt;x-amz-security-token&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;signed&lt;/strong&gt;. They are random, kept in memory only and
never written; a restart ends them and the client asks again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⛔ &lt;strong&gt;Lifetime = min(requested, what the token has left).&lt;/strong&gt; The credentials never
outlive the token that bought them (&lt;code&gt;sts_duration&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;DurationSeconds&lt;/code&gt; up to&lt;code&gt;sts_max_duration&lt;/code&gt;, is only the ceiling). A token with &lt;strong&gt;less than 6 minutes&lt;/strong&gt;
left is refused with &lt;code&gt;ExpiredTokenException&lt;/code&gt;: the AWS SDKs renew about 5
minutes before &lt;code&gt;Expiration&lt;/code&gt;, and shorter credentials would be renewed at once,for ever. A client presents a fresh token at each exchange.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⛔ &lt;strong&gt;A session is judged at every request&lt;/strong&gt;: it expires; its session token is
bound to its access key; it ends when the provider revokes the person after the
token was issued (&lt;a href="https://go-fileshare.github.io/docs/0.51/security/shared-signals/"&gt;shared signals&lt;/a&gt;);and when the configuration stops admitting the name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Policy&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PolicyArns&lt;/code&gt; and a second &lt;code&gt;WebIdentityToken&lt;/code&gt; are refused, and the
parameters must be in the POST body, never the URL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;static_keys = false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; turns the access-key-is-a-user, secret-key-is-the-password
way off. It needs &lt;code&gt;sts = true&lt;/code&gt;: the configuration is refused at load otherwise,since a listener nobody could sign for would look configured. Over a
non-loopback address &lt;code&gt;sts&lt;/code&gt; needs &lt;code&gt;tls = true&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;plaintext = true&lt;/code&gt; when TLS
is terminated in front.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="on-an-unattended-machine-awscred"&gt;On an unattended machine: awscred&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="on-an-unattended-machine-awscred"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#on-an-unattended-machine-awscred" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-authn/awscred" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;code&gt;awscred&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; v0.1.0 is an AWS&lt;code&gt;credential_process&lt;/code&gt; for machines that hold a private key and no password: it
signs a &lt;code&gt;private_key_jwt&lt;/code&gt;, gets a token from go-authn/bridge, calls this
endpoint and prints the credentials as the SDKs read them. The SDKs run it
again before &lt;code&gt;Expiration&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ini" data-lang="ini"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;[profile fileshare]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;credential_process&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s"&gt;awscred --issuer https://login.example.org --client winpc-17 --key /etc/awscred/winpc-17.pem --sts https://s3.example.org&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⛔ On Unix &lt;code&gt;awscred&lt;/code&gt; refuses a key file readable by group or others(&lt;code&gt;chmod 600&lt;/code&gt;). On Windows file modes mean nothing: keep the key in the service
account&amp;rsquo;s profile or in a directory whose ACL admits that account only. A key in
the Windows CNG store or a TPM is not supported yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="behind-a-proxy-trusted_proxies"&gt;Behind a proxy: &lt;code&gt;trusted_proxies&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="behind-a-proxy-trusted_proxies"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#behind-a-proxy-trusted_proxies" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Behind the proxy that &lt;code&gt;plaintext = true&lt;/code&gt; is for, every client would be one
source for the rate limits below. Name the proxies, on the &lt;code&gt;s3&lt;/code&gt; serve block:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-hcl" data-lang="hcl"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;serve&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;s3&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; {
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; addr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;127.0.0.1:9000&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; plaintext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; sts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt; trusted_proxies&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;10.0.0.2&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;10.0.1.0/29&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only a request arriving &lt;strong&gt;from&lt;/strong&gt; a trusted proxy is believed about its client,by the right-most &lt;code&gt;X-Forwarded-For&lt;/code&gt; hop that is not itself a trusted proxy; from
anybody else the header is ignored.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-2 hx:ltr:pr-4 hx:rtl:pl-4 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-amber-200 hx:bg-amber-100 hx:text-amber-900 hx:dark:border-amber-200/30 hx:dark:bg-amber-900/30 hx:dark:text-amber-200"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:ltr:pl-3 hx:ltr:pr-2 hx:rtl:pr-3 hx:rtl:pl-2"&gt;&lt;svg height=1.2em class="hx:inline-block hx:align-middle" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7"&gt;
&lt;div class="hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The list must name the proxies and nothing else&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A prefix wider than one host (a &lt;code&gt;/24&lt;/code&gt;, an IPv6 &lt;code&gt;/64&lt;/code&gt;) is accepted — a pool of
proxies, a &lt;code&gt;/29&lt;/code&gt;, is legitimate — and a warning is printed at start: a client
that can have an address inside it chooses its own &lt;code&gt;X-Forwarded-For&lt;/code&gt;, and with
it the bucket it is counted in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="limits"&gt;Limits&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="limits"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#limits" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;16 sessions per name&lt;/strong&gt;: the oldest of the same name goes first, another
name&amp;rsquo;s sessions stay (20000 in all).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;60 requests a minute per source address&lt;/strong&gt;, answered &lt;code&gt;429 Throttling&lt;/code&gt;. Every
request counts, valid or not, before the token is verified. A source is an
IPv4 address, or an IPv6 &lt;strong&gt;/64&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The count is O(1) per request, under its own lock, in a sliding minute made
of two generations; the credentialed S3 requests never wait for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A source seen in the last minute is counted as long as the table holds fewer
than &lt;strong&gt;2 × 10000&lt;/strong&gt; entries (the bound, however long a flood lasts). A source
the full table has not seen is counted in an overflow bucket of its network —its &lt;strong&gt;/48&lt;/strong&gt; (IPv6) or &lt;strong&gt;/24&lt;/strong&gt; (IPv4), ten times the rate each — so a flood
exhausts the buckets of the networks it comes from, not everybody&amp;rsquo;s. IPv4
neighbours behind one /24 (CGNAT, a campus) share one bucket.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⛔ &lt;strong&gt;Past 1024 networks a minute, one shared bucket serves the rest&lt;/strong&gt;: an
attacker holding more networks than that exhausts it, and every source the
table has not already seen — &lt;strong&gt;existing clients that renew about hourly
included&lt;/strong&gt; — is refused until the minute turns. That is this design&amp;rsquo;s limit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="two-limits-worth-knowing-before-pointing-it-at-something-large"&gt;Two limits worth knowing before pointing it at something large&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="two-limits-worth-knowing-before-pointing-it-at-something-large"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#two-limits-worth-knowing-before-pointing-it-at-something-large" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;GetObject&lt;/code&gt; reads the whole object into memory.&lt;/strong&gt; The driver interface offers&lt;code&gt;ReadFile&lt;/code&gt; and nothing else — no opener, no reader — so there is no streaming
read to use. A bound, 256 MiB, answers &lt;code&gt;EntityTooLarge&lt;/code&gt; rather than taking
the process down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;LastModified&lt;/code&gt; is the epoch.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;filesystem.Stat&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;Mode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Size&lt;/code&gt; and&lt;code&gt;Inode&lt;/code&gt;, and no modification time at all. The field is not optional in the S3
schema, so something must be sent; the epoch is obviously not a real time,where &lt;code&gt;time.Now()&lt;/code&gt; would look like a file that just changed and make every sync
tool copy everything, every run.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>